---
// Runs where you work: the interfaces and the models, condensed to three rows each.
---

<section class="band alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="band-head">
      <h2>Runs where you work. On any model — even yours.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="flex2">
      <div class="flexcol">
        <h3>Interfaces</h3>
        <p class="sub">One engine, many surfaces — connect your agent in one command.</p>
        <div class="flexrow"><div class="name"><b>Any MCP client</b><span>Claude Code &amp; Desktop, Cursor, Codex, Gemini CLI, VS Code — stdio or HTTP</span></div><span class="pill ok">supported</span></div>
        <div class="flexrow"><div class="name"><b>CLI &amp; TUI</b><span>the standalone Turf agent: <code>chat</code>, <code>up</code>, <code>destroy</code> — bring your own model</span></div><span class="pill ok">supported</span></div>
        <div class="flexrow"><div class="name"><b>Kubernetes, in-cluster</b><span>deployed as an agent via kagent, state in the cluster</span></div><span class="pill ok">supported</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="flexcol">
        <h3>Models</h3>
        <p class="sub">The standalone agent runs on any model; your MCP client brings its own.</p>
        <div class="flexrow"><div class="name"><b>Hosted frontier models</b><span>Anthropic, Google, and OpenAI-compatible endpoints</span></div><span class="pill ok">supported</span></div>
        <div class="flexrow"><div class="name"><b>Local models</b><span><code>turf --model dmr/ai/qwen3</code> — no API key, no cost</span></div><span class="pill ok">supported</span></div>
        <div class="flexrow"><div class="name"><b>Private GPU clouds</b><span>vLLM, LM Studio, gateways via <code>--base-url</code></span></div><span class="pill ok">supported</span></div>
        <p class="kicker">Your infrastructure intent never has to leave your network.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
